#: ../../../driver-api/issei/issei.rst:4
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/issei/issei.rst:6
msgid ""
"The Intel Silicon Security Engine (Intel SSE) is an isolated and protected "
"computing resource (Co-processor) residing inside Intel client chipsets "
"released in 2024 (Lunar Lake) or later. The Intel SSE provide security "
"support and platform boot orchestration. The actual feature set depends on "
"the Intel chipset SKU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/issei/issei.rst:12
msgid ""
"The Intel Silicon Security Engine Interface (Intel SSEI) is the interface "
"between the Host and Intel SSE. This interface is exposed to the host as one "
"or more PCI devices. The Intel SSEI Driver is in charge of the communication "
"channel between a host application and the Intel SSE features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/issei/issei.rst:18
msgid ""
"Each Intel SSE feature, or Intel SSE Client is addressed by a unique UUID "
"and each client has its own protocol. The protocol is message-based with a "
"header and payload up to maximal number of bytes advertised by the client, "
"upon connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/issei/issei.rst:24
msgid "Intel SSEI Driver"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/issei/issei.rst:26
msgid "The driver exposes a character device with device nodes /dev/isseiX."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/issei/issei.rst:28
msgid ""
"An application maintains communication with an Intel SSE feature while /dev/"
"isseiX is open. The binding to a specific feature is performed by calling :c:"
"macro:`IOCTL_ISSEI_CONNECT_CLIENT`, which passes the desired UUID. The "
"number of instances of an Intel SSE feature that can be opened at the same "
"time is limited to single instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/issei/issei.rst:34
msgid ""
"The driver is transparent to data that are passed between firmware feature "
"and host application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/issei/issei.rst:37
msgid ""
"Because some of the Intel SSE features can change the system configuration, "
"the driver by default allows only a privileged user to access it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/issei/issei.rst:41
msgid ""
"The connection termination is performed by calling :c:macro:"
"`IOCTL_ISSEI_DISCONNECT_CLIENT`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/issei/issei.rst:44
msgid "The session is terminated calling :c:expr:`close(fd)`."
msgstr ""

